Web source (THE spec): web/src/features/admin/components/devtools/tools/RegexTester.tsx
  Self-contained client-side tool. Only hook = useTranslation (no networked P1/S8 store).
  Inputs: pattern, flags (g/gi/gm/gim/""), testStr. Derives matches via JS RegExp(pattern, flags):
  global -> all matches, else first; `if (!m[0]) break` zero-width guard; invalid -> catch -> [].
  Renders: ToolCard header (icon+title+desc, red), Pattern Input, Flags Select, Test String Textarea,
  "{n} Matches" Badge, and a per-match list (ordinal Badge, monospaced match, "At Index {i}").

Native output (apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/RegexTester.*):
  RegexTester.Adapter.swift   — pure Foundation evaluator + projection (RegexEvaluation/RegexPhase) + a11y
  RegexTester.Model.swift     — P1/S11 telemetry seam (view.opened), @Observable state holder, P1/S10 i18n facade
  RegexTester.swift           — SwiftUI tool-card surface (surfaceSlug="RegexTester"); renders every branch
  RegexTester.Views.swift     — subviews: result chip, match list/row, inline idle/no-match/invalid, field chrome
  RegexTester.Previews.swift  — DEBUG previews for every state
  RegexTester.strings         — P1/S10 i18n catalog (table "RegexTester")
  RegexTester.Tests.swift     — XCTest: adapter + model phases + telemetry + a11y

States reproduced (faithful to the web source's actual branches): idle (no input), matches, noMatches
  (valid pattern, zero matches), invalidPattern (the web `catch` path, surfaced accessibly rather than
  silently hidden). loading/stale/offline are intentionally NOT fabricated — this is pure local compute
  with no async Resource<T>; inventing those surfaces would be a parity lie (Honesty Covenant #3/#5).

